  "id": "forward-fast-pogo-shuffle",
  "name": "Forward Fast Pogo Shuffle",
  "definition": "A forward-travelling rapid shuffle on the balls of the feet with alternating brief foot contacts as a practical interpretation of the source-described shuffle, slight knee flexion, heels low, and hands on hips. The Boxing Science library recommends 10–15 seconds; the current power catalog supports repetition tracking only, so each alternating contact is logged as a rep as a product convention and duration is given as practice guidance. This is not a simultaneous stationary vertical pogo or a maximal-height jump. The intentionally small hip and knee motions control forward travel without making a lunge or squat repetition. Ankle and knee contributions are frequency-dependent; no tendon or boxing-performance outcome is claimed.",
